.TH SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_ALPHA 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_ALPHA \- A macro to determine if an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
has an alpha channel.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pixels.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_ALPHA(format)   \(rs
.BI "    ((SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_PACKED(format) && \(rs
.BI "      ((SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_PACKEDORDER_ARGB) || \(rs
.BI "       (SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_PACKEDORDER_RGBA) || \(rs
.BI "       (SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_PACKEDORDER_ABGR) || \(rs
.BI "       (SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_PACKEDORDER_BGRA))) || \(rs
.BI "     (SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_ARRAY(format) && \(rs
.BI "      ((SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_ARRAYORDER_ARGB) || \(rs
.BI "       (SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_ARRAYORDER_RGBA) || \(rs
.BI "       (SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_ARRAYORDER_ABGR) || \(rs
.BI "       (SDL_PIXELORDER(format) == SDL_ARRAYORDER_BGRA))))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that this macro double-evaluates its parameter, so do not use expressions with side-effects here\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I format
an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
to check\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if the format has alpha, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

